From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ActivityManagerService: don't compact system processes 20 minutes after boot

A CAF change carried by crDroid since 14.0 (30306f98c8e7 there,
"CachedAppOptimizer: Set thread group to background") added
CachedAppOptimizer.compactAllSystem() to the task that runs
FULL_PSS_MIN_INTERVAL (20 minutes) after the user's boot completes.
AOSP does not compact system processes there or anywhere else on its
own: a93181541fda ("ActivityManagerService: don't compact system at
BOOT_COMPLETED") took it out of the boot path, and the remaining call in
performIdleMaintenance() is behind disable_system_compaction, which is
enabled in release builds. The CAF call bypasses that flag, so it is the
only automatic system compaction left on crDroid.

With useMemcgForCompaction, compactAllSystem() writes the whole
memory.current of the system cgroup to its memory.reclaim, so every
system daemon is reclaimed at once, whatever the device is doing at that
moment. SurfaceFlinger, the composer HAL, audioserver and the audio HAL
then fault their working set back in while the reclaim is still running.
On the Huawei MateBook E Go during a rhythm game this shows as about one
second of heavy frame drops and, without swap, speaker crackle; with zram
the audio stays clean, but composition still misses frames for about
half a second.

Drop the call and keep the deferred PSS collection, as in AOSP and
LineageOS. System processes are then compacted only on request
(am compact system); cached app compaction is unchanged.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 .../core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java  | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java
index e40aea8..0e2ef33 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/am/ActivityManagerService.java
@@ -6011,7 +6011,6 @@ public class ActivityManagerService extends IActivityManager.Stub
                             // Defer the full Pss collection as the system is really busy now.
                             mHandler.postDelayed(() -> {
                                 synchronized (mProcLock) {
-                                    mCachedAppOptimizer.compactAllSystem();
                                     mAppProfiler.requestPssAllProcsLPr(
                                             SystemClock.uptimeMillis(), true, false);
                                 }
